WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.133
-Today is Friday.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.868
That's usually when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.133
I check my in-box
or I check my e-mails.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.100
I send thank-you notes.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.601
And I was just running --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:12.868
I was running
a bit behind today.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.367
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.334
Anyways, I'd like to write out
some thank-you notes right now.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.434
Is that cool with you guys?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:20.534
James, can I get some

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:21.901
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.200
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.300
-Wow. Look at that.
-Wow!

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.167
-Thank you, Three Wise Men
bringing gifts of

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.868
gold, frankincense, and myrrh,
for showing us

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.000
you clearly never have been
to a baby shower.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.667
It's like, "Diapers. Diapers."

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.968
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:51.100
Thank you, tinsel, for showing
me what my tree would look like

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.901
if it went through
a '70s glam-rock phase.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.701
-Nice!
-Yeah.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.400
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.133
Thank you, Christmas,
for being that special time

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.434
we reflect on
the Holy Trinity --

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.534
regular, cheesy, and caramel.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.801
Mix them both. Oh, you rebel!

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.968
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:21.701
Thank you, Christmas lawn
inflatables in the morning,

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.534
for looking like Frosty
went a little too hard

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.267
the night before.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:27.667
-Oh, no!

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.868
-[ Yawns ]
Leave me alone.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.300
"Wake up, wake up, Frosty."

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.367
-Blow me up.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.334
-Ugh!

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.734
-Mm, Frosty!

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:40.067
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.701
-Thank you, Christmas dinner,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.634
for basically
panicking and being like,

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.567
"Uh, let's just do
Thanksgiving again, plus ham.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.067
Yeah, that's what we'll do.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:50.434
I don't know. Sure."

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.334
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:56.901
Thank you, stores that offer
gift wrapping,

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.200
for being a fun way of asking,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.300
"Hey, want to be stuck here
for an extra 40 minutes?"

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.534
I guess so.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.567
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.033
Thank you,
wrapping gifts yourself,

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:14.434
for taking 10 seconds to go from
"This is coming out great" to

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.734
"I mean, I don't need to
cover the whole box."

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.267
No one looks at the bottom.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.267
-Come on, it looks gorgeous.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.701
Take a picture of it, yeah.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:25.167
And save that wrapping paper.
I want to use it next year.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.033
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:33.300
Thank you, eggnog, for easily
being one of the top-five nogs.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.601
Easily.
-Easily, yeah.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.167
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.701
-Thank you,
Rudolph saving Christmas,

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:43.901
for proving that Santa can make
truly anything in his workshop,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.634
as long as it's not headlights.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:52.601
"Rudolph, you get
in front, and --"

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:55.000
"Huh?"
-Oh, no!

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.367
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:59.767
-Thank you, sugarplums,
for sounding suspiciously like

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:03.167
someone just trying to
rebrand prunes.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.000
"Uh, they're sugarplums.

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:11.434
-Is that the last one of 2021?

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:14.534
-[ Chuckles ]
Wow.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.033
This is the last one of 2021.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.167
We're all here together,
sharing this experience.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.267
-♪ A shared experience ♪

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.234
-I know. I love it. So happy.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:26.734
Well, I want to thank each
and every one of you

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:29.334
for coming out tonight
and laughing...

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.067
...cheering...

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.367
...hooting...

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.133
[ Audience hoots ]

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.501
...hollering...

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:42.234
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.434
...yelling.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:45.434
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.033
Whispering...

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:54.667
...loving...
-Aww!

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.701
-...caring...
-Ooh!

00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:01.367
-...being jealous...
-Ah!

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.367
-...being...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.267
Yes.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.133
[ Soft music playing ]

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:14.267
Thank you, Santa Claus,
for festively testing

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.167
the limits of
breaking-and-entering laws.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:17.667
There you have it, everybody.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.300
That's our last
"Thank You Note" of 2021.

